[Music]  this  is breaking news on eight news now  now at five governor steve sisselak has  tested positive for covid19 that  announcement coming into our newsroom  about an hour ago i'm brian loftis and  i'm denise valdez the governor says he  underwent routine testing today  and a rapid test did give him that  positive result  our vanessa murphy is following the  story and has more details for us  tonight vanessa  governor siselek is currently in  quarantine at the governor's mansion  up north he says he does not currently  have covet 19 symptoms but  he did previously feel fatigued he  thought he was just tired  he has a busy schedule now he gets  tested  at least once a week though his last two  tests on november 6  and november 2nd came back negative the  latest test with the positive results as  you mentioned  is a rapid test he's still waiting for  the results of a pcr test which does not  provide  immediate results now because of the  positive test the governor will be  checking in with a physician regularly  a spokeswoman says his wife tested  negative for covid19  the governor personally called other  close contacts at this time  staff from the governor's office will  also be in quarantine  earlier this week sisilak attended a  ribbon cutting and also he held a press  conference  about a spike in covid 19 cases  in our state now the governor made a  post on facebook he says he's using this  as an opportunity to remind nevadans to  stay home  and he referred to the numbers in nevada  the more than  1800 new cases identified in nevada  yesterday  and he says cases are growing at a rate  of 1.3 percent  or about 1400 new cases  per day now it appears the governor is  one of these new cases  reporting live vanessa murphy 8 news now

